  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:2574",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to interact with cAMP-dependent protein kinase catalytic subunit beta through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C targets Serine/threonine-protein kinase ICK, which is a known target of Ent-Gloeosteretriol. Ent-Gloeosteretriol, in turn, has a direct target relationship with cAMP-dependent protein kinase catalytic subunit beta. Similarly, Oblonganoside C also targets Caov-4 and NCI-H1734, which are both targets of Ent-Gloeosteretriol, reinforcing the link to the same downstream effector. These findings collectively imply that Oblonganoside C modulates the activity of cAMP-dependent protein kinase through Ent-Gloeosteretriol, suggesting a potential mechanism involving the activation of this kinase pathway. The evidence supports a central role for Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a mediator in the interaction between Oblonganoside C and the cAMP-dependent protein kinase catalytic subunit beta.",
